{"id":8412226417108,"type":"genre","name":"Indie Rock","n":4},{"id":223327500886715,"type":"genre","name":"Contemporary Folk","n":3},{"id":194427380844280,"type":"genre","name":"Folk Rock","n":2},{"id":266148395847073,"type":"genre","name":"Synth Punk","n":1},{"id":242270330474188,"type":"genre","name":"Country Soul","n":1},{"id":236061900877969,"type":"genre","name":"Chamber Pop","n":1},{"id":219217594239320,"type":"genre","name":"Folk Metal","n":1},{"id":212257394657788,"type":"genre","name":"Gipsy Punk","n":1},{"id":207755761847598,"type":"genre","name":"Hardcore","n":1},{"id":200651337068219,"type":"genre","name":"Canzone d'autore","n":1},{"id":191043281221162,"type":"genre","name":"Brutal Prog","n":1}],"labels":[],"album_labels":[],"own_scenes":[],"scenes":[{"id":4419681145361,"name":"Cantautores lo-fi de los noventa","book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","start":1990,"end":2003,"desc":"Los noventa son la década del cantautor: la tecnología y las redes informales del post-punk favorecen la carrera en solitario, con Joni Mitchell y Leonard Cohen (no Dylan ni Springsteen) como maestros. El folk sombrío inaugurado por Chris Isaak, Smog y American Music Club se convierte casi en un género: Vic Chesnutt, Mark Lanegan, Mountain Goats, Elliott Smith, Jeff Buckley, Ron Sexsmith, Mike Johnson, Simon Joyner, Songs:Ohia. El neo-pop de Stephen Merritt (Magnetic Fields: Holiday, The Charm Of The Highway Strip, 69 Love Songs), Chris Connelly, Frank Black, Mike Gira (Body Lovers, Angels Of Light), Richard Davies y Eric Matthews (Cardinal), David Gray. El neo-folk de Beck (folk para la era del hip hop), John Frusciante, Sparklehorse, Bright Eyes, Rufus Wainwright, Grandaddy, Bobby Conn; el neo-country de Richard Buckner y Freedy Johnston; Steve Wynn, Mike Watt, Paul Westerberg, Ben Harper.","color":"#a3e635","family":"Folk y cantautores","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#songwriters-90s"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":158799467845461,"artist":"Elliott Smith","artist_id":194215321578954,"title":"Roman Candle","year":1994,"ess":0,"yt":"04N7KRC728M","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Cantautores lo-fi de los noventa","scene_id":4419681145361,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#songwriters-90s","chapters":["Sección 6.6"],"pages":[[1,247,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":247,"text":"…mostly about disintegrating relationships, which were as lyrically ambitious as musically humble. In Oregon, Heatmiser's singer and songwriter Elliott Smith (1) employed spare, acoustic arrangements and anemically whispered lyrics on Roman Candle (1994) to pen tuneful vignettes of daily life that merged…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":281,"text":"…that fell into the category during the 1990s included: San Francisco's Jawbreaker, with Unfun (1990); Oregon's Heatmiser, the group of songwriter Elliott Smith, with Dead Air (1993); Los Angeles' Weezer, the most successful of the batch, with Weezer (1994); Seattle's Sunny Day Real Estate (1), the vehicle…"}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Case Remains Open with LAPD","body":"The case of Elliot Smith's death continues to be classified as open by the LAPD, reflecting the lingering uncertainties and the lack of a definitive conclusion regarding the circumstances of his passing. \"Today, the case remains open with the LAPD.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Rock Stars Who Were Murdered","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q6dAX6HCjgw"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Death by Two Stab Wounds","body":"Elliot Smith died on October 21, 2003, at the age of 34, from two stab wounds to the chest. The incident occurred during an argument with his girlfriend, Jennifer, where he reportedly threatened suicide. Jennifer found him with a kitchen knife sticking out of his chest, pulled it out, and called 911, but he later died in the hospital. \"Smith died on October 21, 2003. There were two stab wounds in his chest, even fighting with his girlfriend, Jennifer, during which time he threatened to commit suicide.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Rock Stars Who Were Murdered","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q6dAX6HCjgw"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Influential Indie Artist of the 1990s","body":"Elliot Smith, despite not selling a large volume of records, remains deeply loved by his fans and is considered one of the most influential indie artists of the 1990s. His unique style left a lasting impact on the music scene. \"Elliot Smith never sold a lot of records, but he remains deeply, deeply loved by his fans. And he's also considered to be one of the most influential indie artists of the 1990s.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Rock Stars Who Were Murdered","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q6dAX6HCjgw"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Post-Mortem Praise","body":"Elliot Smith is mentioned as an artist who received praise, alongside Nick Drake and Jeff Buckley, implying a similar post-mortem recognition or heightened appreciation. \"Potser Mous Praise for Nick Drake, Jeff Buckley, and Elliot Smith.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"What's the Big Deal About Joy Division?","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1VWJ0uCQx8w"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Songs About David Berkowitz","body":"Elliot Smith is mentioned as one of the artists who have written songs about David Berkowitz, the Son of Sam killer. \"They come from everyone from the Beastie Boys to Elliot Smith to Lana Del Rey.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Murder Ballads (and Other Deadly Songs)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FtGJHhqXcDI"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Suspicion of Murder Despite Suicide Note","body":"Despite a suicide note and a history of ADHD, depression, suicidal ideation, drug use, and heavy drinking, police, the coroner, and fans remained suspicious of Elliot Smith's death. The primary reason for this suspicion was the absence of \"hesitation wounds,\" as he had stabbed himself cleanly twice directly in the heart. \"Police were still suspicious. The corner was suspicious and fans remain suspicious. Why? Mainly because there were no hesitation wounds.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Rock Stars Who Were Murdered","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q6dAX6HCjgw"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Unusual Nature of Stab Wounds","body":"The method of Elliot Smith's death, two clean stabs directly to the heart without hesitation, is highly unusual for suicide. Statistics indicate that only 4% of suicides involve sharp force trauma, predominantly wrist-slashing. The act of turning a knife sideways and plunging it between the ribs twice without hesitation is considered an extremely painful way to die, fueling theories among fans that \"bad drug buddies\" might have been involved. \"According to statistics on suicide, only 4% of people take their own lives with sharp force trauma and almost all of those involve wrist-slashing.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Rock Stars Who Were Murdered","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q6dAX6HCjgw"}]}],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":158799467845461,"type":"album","name":"Roman Candle","list_id":118267099057662,"list":"AOTY Must Hear 1990s","src":"musthear","rank":281,"year":1994,"note":null,"yt":"DCZbnvzRUjQ","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":158799467845461,"type":"album","name":"Roman Candle","list_id":94905110718967,"list":"RYM Top — Fo